        "content": "# Hypothesis Document: yaml-validator-command\n**Version**: 1.0.0 | **Created**: 2026-03-17T18:46:00Z | **Status**: VALIDATED\n\n## Hypotheses\n### HYP-001: Bun provides built-in YAML parsing without external dependencies\n**Risk Level**: HIGH\n**Status**: CONFIRMED\n**Statement**: Bun has a built-in YAML parser (e.g., Bun.YAML, bun:yaml module, or similar) that can parse YAML strings without adding external npm dependencies.\n**Context**: The yaml-validator-command feature needs to parse YAML files. If Bun lacks built-in YAML support, an external dependency like `js-yaml` or `yaml` would be required, impacting the project's zero-dependency architecture.\n**Validation Criteria**:\n- CONFIRM if: Bun exposes a YAML parsing API (e.g., `Bun.YAML.parse()`) that successfully parses valid YAML strings into JavaScript objects\n- REJECT if: No built-in YAML parsing capability exists and an external library is required\n**Suggested Method**: CODE_EXPERIMENT\n\n### HYP-002: Bun's YAML parser provides error location information (line/column numbers)\n**Risk Level**: MEDIUM\n**Status**: REJECTED\n**Statement**: When Bun's YAML parser encounters invalid YAML, the thrown error includes line and column number information pointing to the location within the YAML content where the error occurred.\n**Context**: The yaml-validator-command needs to provide helpful error messages that tell users where in their YAML file the problem is. Without line/column information, error messages will be vague and less useful.\n**Validation Criteria**:\n- CONFIRM if: The SyntaxError thrown by Bun.YAML.parse() contains properties or message text indicating the line/column within the YAML content where parsing failed\n- REJECT if: The error only contains generic messages without YAML-content-specific location information\n**Suggested Method**: CODE_EXPERIMENT\n\n## Validation Findings\n\n### HYP-001 Findings\n**Validated**: 2026-03-17T18:47:00Z\n**Method**: CODE_EXPERIMENT\n**Result**: CONFIRMED\n\n**Evidence**:\nBun (version 1.3.3) provides a fully functional built-in YAML parser via `Bun.YAML`. The API was introduced in Bun 1.2.21 (August 2025).\n\n1. **`Bun.YAML` object exists** with two methods: `parse` and `stringify`\n2. **`Bun.YAML.parse(yamlString)`** successfully parses YAML strings into JavaScript objects, supporting:\n   - Scalars (strings, numbers, booleans, null)\n   - Nested mappings (objects)\n   - Sequences (arrays)\n   - All standard YAML 1.2 types\n3. **`Bun.YAML.stringify(obj)`** is also available for serialization\n4. **Import syntax**: Both `Bun.YAML.parse()` and `import { YAML } from \"bun\"` work correctly\n5. **Direct file imports**: Bun supports `import config from \"./config.yaml\"` with named exports\n\nExperiment output (truncated):\n```\ntypeof Bun.YAML: object\ntypeof Bun.YAML.parse: function\ntypeof Bun.YAML.stringify: function\n\nParsed successfully: {\n  \"name\": \"test-project\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0.0\",\n  \"database\": { \"host\": \"localhost\", \"port\": 5432, ... },\n  \"tags\": [\"typescript\", \"bun\", \"yaml\"],\n  \"enabled\": true,\n  \"count\": 42,\n  \"ratio\": 3.14,\n  \"nothing\": null\n}\n```\n\n**Sources**:\n- https://bun.com/docs/runtime/yaml\n- https://bun.com/reference/bun/YAML\n- Code experiment: `/tmp/hypothesis-yaml-validator-command/test-hyp-001.ts`\n\n**Implications for Design**:\nThe feature can use `Bun.YAML.parse()` directly with zero external dependencies, fully consistent with the project's architecture (no dependencies beyond Bun built-ins). Both `parse` and `stringify` are available natively.\n\n---\n\n### HYP-002 Findings\n**Validated**: 2026-03-17T18:48:00Z\n**Method**: CODE_EXPERIMENT\n**Result**: REJECTED\n\n**Evidence**:\nBun's YAML parser does NOT provide error location information within the YAML content. Extensive testing reveals:\n\n1. **Error type**: `SyntaxError` is thrown on invalid YAML (as documented)\n2. **Error message**: Generic messages only -- e.g., `\"YAML Parse error: Unexpected token\"`, `\"YAML Parse error: Unexpected character\"`. No line/column numbers embedded in the message text.\n3. **Error properties**: The SyntaxError has these own properties: `message`, `originalLine`, `originalColumn`, `line`, `column`, `sourceURL`, `stack`\n4. **CRITICAL FINDING**: The `line`/`column` and `originalLine`/`originalColumn` properties reference the **TypeScript source file** location where `Bun.YAML.parse()` was called, NOT the location within the YAML content.\n\nProof via controlled experiment:\n```\n// Same invalid YAML called from two different TS file locations:\nTest 1: Parse called from TS line ~13  -> error.line=15, error.originalLine=10\nTest 2: Parse called from TS line ~25  -> error.line=29, error.originalLine=18\n// line/column changes with call site, not with YAML content\n\n// Different YAML strings with errors at different YAML lines:\nYAML error on content line 4 (called from TS line ~13) -> error.line=15\nYAML error on content line 10 (called from TS line ~63) -> error.line=74\n// No correlation with YAML content line numbers\n```\n\n5. **No hidden properties**: Deep inspection of the error object (including prototype chain, all property names, and common error location property names from other parsers) found no YAML-content-specific location data.\n6. **`Bun.YAML.parse` signature**: Accepts exactly 1 argument (the string). No options/configuration parameter available.\n7. **Known issues**: Multiple GitHub issues confirm YAML parser limitations in Bun 1.2.x-1.3.x, and no mention of error location features in any issue or documentation.\n\n**Sources**:\n- Code experiment: `/tmp/hypothesis-yaml-validator-command/test-hyp-002.ts`\n- Code experiment: `/tmp/hypothesis-yaml-validator-command/test-hyp-002b.ts`\n- Code experiment: `/tmp/hypothesis-yaml-validator-command/test-hyp-002c.ts`\n- https://github.com/oven-sh/bun/issues/22659\n- https://github.com/oven-sh/bun/issues/22392\n- https://github.com/oven-sh/bun/issues/23489\n\n**Implications for Design**:\nThe feature cannot rely on Bun's built-in parser for detailed error location reporting. Design options:\n1. **Accept generic errors**: Use `Bun.YAML.parse()` and report the error message without line/column info. Users get \"YAML Parse error: Unexpected token\" but no location.\n2. **Add an external YAML library** (e.g., `js-yaml` or `yaml` npm package) which provides rich error objects with `mark.line`, `mark.column`, and contextual snippets. This trades the zero-dependency goal for better error quality.\n3. **Hybrid approach**: Use `Bun.YAML.parse()` for validation (fast, zero-dep), and if it fails, optionally use a fallback parser to extract location info. This adds complexity but preserves the fast path.\n4. **Custom line detection**: Parse the generic error message and attempt to locate the issue by re-parsing line-by-line. Fragile and unreliable.\n\n## Summary\n| Hypothesis | Risk | Result | Implication |\n|------------|------|--------|-------------|\n| HYP-001: Bun built-in YAML parser | HIGH | CONFIRMED | Zero-dependency YAML parsing available via `Bun.YAML.parse()` and `Bun.YAML.stringify()` |\n| HYP-002: Error location info | MEDIUM | REJECTED | Parser errors lack YAML-content line/column info; only generic messages provided |\n"
