        "file_path": "/private/tmp/rp1-evals/32de8016/workspace/.rp1/work/features/yaml-validator-command/tasks.md",
        "content": "# Development Tasks: YAML Validator Command\n\n**Feature ID**: yaml-validator-command\n**Status**: Not Started\n**Progress**: 0% (0 of 7 tasks)\n**Estimated Effort**: 2 days\n**Started**: 2026-03-17\n\n## Overview\n\nA CLI command that validates YAML file syntax using Bun's built-in YAML support (`Bun.YAML.parse()`). The command accepts file paths as arguments, validates each for YAML syntax correctness, and reports human-readable results with appropriate exit codes. Error messages will be generic (parser error text only) since Bun's YAML parser does not provide line/column location information (HYP-002 rejected).\n\n## Implementation DAG\n\n**Parallel Groups** (tasks with no inter-dependencies):\n\n1. [T1] - Foundation module with no internal dependencies\n2. [T2, T3, T4] - All depend on T1 interfaces but are independent of each other\n\n**Dependencies**:\n\n- T2 -> T1 (Interface: CLI imports `validateYamlFile` from yaml-validator)\n- T3 -> T1 (Interface: Tests import `validateYamlFile`, `validateYamlContent` from yaml-validator)\n- T4 -> T2 (Sequential: Script entry references `src/validate-yaml.ts` which must exist)\n\n**Critical Path**: T1 -> T2 -> T4\n\n## Task Breakdown\n\n### Foundation - Validation Logic\n\n- [ ] **T1**: Implement YAML validation logic module (`src/yaml-validator.ts`) with `validateYamlFile` and `validateYamlContent` exported functions using `Bun.YAML.parse()` `[complexity:medium]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#32-module-srcyaml-validatorts-validation-logic](design.md#32-module-srcyaml-validatorts-validation-logic)\n\n    **Effort**: 4 hours\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] File `src/yaml-validator.ts` exists and exports `validateYamlFile(filePath: string) => Promise<ValidationResult>` function\n    - [ ] File exports `validateYamlContent(content: string, filePath: string) => ValidationResult` function\n    - [ ] `ValidationResult` interface is exported with fields: `filePath`, `valid`, `error?`, `line?`, `column?`\n    - [ ] `validateYamlFile` reads file using `Bun.file(filePath).text()` and returns `{ valid: false, error: \"File not found or unreadable: <path>\" }` on read failure\n    - [ ] Empty files (zero-length or whitespace-only) return `{ valid: true }` per BR-002\n    - [ ] `validateYamlContent` splits content on `---` document separators and validates each segment individually per BR-003\n    - [ ] YAML parsing uses `Bun.YAML.parse()` (HYP-001 confirmed; zero new dependencies per FR-005)\n    - [ ] Error messages use the parser's native error text only; no line/column extraction is attempted (HYP-002 rejected: Bun.YAML.parse() does not provide location info)\n    - [ ] Module contains no side effects (no console output, no process.exit)\n\n### CLI and Integration\n\n- [ ] **T2**: Implement CLI entry point (`src/validate-yaml.ts`) with argument parsing, output formatting, and exit code logic `[complexity:medium]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#33-module-srcvalidate-yamlts-cli-entry-point](design.md#33-module-srcvalidate-yamlts-cli-entry-point)\n\n    **Effort**: 4 hours\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] File `src/validate-yaml.ts` exists and imports `validateYamlFile` from `./yaml-validator`\n    - [ ] `parseArgs` function extracts file paths from `process.argv.slice(2)` and detects `--help`/`-h` flags\n    - [ ] `showUsage` function prints usage information to stdout including at least one example invocation (FR-006)\n    - [ ] Running with no file arguments displays usage and exits with code 1\n    - [ ] Running with `--help` or `-h` displays usage and exits with code 0\n    - [ ] `formatResult` outputs `PASS  <path>` for valid files and `FAIL  <path>` with indented error detail for invalid files\n    - [ ] When multiple files are validated, a summary line is printed: `Results: N passed, M failed`\n    - [ ] Exit code is 0 when all files are valid; exit code is 1 when any file is invalid or unreadable (FR-003)\n    - [ ] All remaining files continue to be processed after a failure (FR-004 AC-2)\n\n- [ ] **T3**: Implement unit tests for validation logic (`src/yaml-validator.test.ts`) covering valid, invalid, empty, multi-doc, and missing file cases `[complexity:medium]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#7-testing-strategy](design.md#7-testing-strategy)\n\n    **Effort**: 4 hours\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] File `src/yaml-validator.test.ts` exists and uses `bun:test` test runner\n    - [ ] Test: `validateYamlContent` returns valid for correct YAML input\n    - [ ] Test: `validateYamlContent` returns valid for empty content (BR-002)\n    - [ ] Test: `validateYamlContent` returns invalid with error details for malformed YAML\n    - [ ] Test: `validateYamlContent` validates all documents in multi-document YAML (BR-003)\n    - [ ] Test: `validateYamlContent` returns invalid if any document in multi-doc YAML is malformed\n    - [ ] Test: `validateYamlFile` returns valid for a valid YAML file (uses temp file)\n    - [ ] Test: `validateYamlFile` returns invalid for an invalid YAML file (uses temp file)\n    - [ ] Test: `validateYamlFile` returns error for non-existent file path\n    - [ ] Test: `validateYamlFile` returns valid for an empty file (uses temp file)\n    - [ ] All tests pass with `bun test`\n\n- [ ] **T4**: Register `validate-yaml` script in `package.json` pointing to `src/validate-yaml.ts` `[complexity:simple]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#8-deployment-design](design.md#8-deployment-design)\n\n    **Effort**: 1 hour\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] `package.json` `scripts` object contains `\"validate-yaml\": \"bun run src/validate-yaml.ts\"`\n    - [ ] Running `bun run validate-yaml --help` displays usage information\n    - [ ] No new entries in `dependencies` or `devDependencies` (FR-005)\n\n### User Docs\n\n- [ ] **TD1**: Update modules documentation - Modules `[complexity:simple]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#documentation-impact](design.md#documentation-impact)\n\n    **Type**: edit\n\n    **Target**: `.rp1/context/modules.md`\n\n    **Section**: Modules\n\n    **KB Source**: modules.md\n\n    **Effort**: 30 minutes\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] Section reflects new `yaml-validator` and `validate-yaml` module entries with descriptions\n\n- [ ] **TD2**: Update architecture documentation - Scripts `[complexity:simple]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#documentation-impact](design.md#documentation-impact)\n\n    **Type**: edit\n\n    **Target**: `.rp1/context/architecture.md`\n\n    **Section**: Scripts\n\n    **KB Source**: architecture.md\n\n    **Effort**: 30 minutes\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] Section reflects the new `validate-yaml` script entry\n\n- [ ] **TD3**: Update project index - Project Structure `[complexity:simple]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#documentation-impact](design.md#documentation-impact)\n\n    **Type**: edit\n\n    **Target**: `.rp1/context/index.md`\n\n    **Section**: Project Structure\n\n    **KB Source**: index.md\n\n    **Effort**: 30 minutes\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] New files (`src/yaml-validator.ts`, `src/validate-yaml.ts`, `src/yaml-validator.test.ts`) are listed in the src/ directory listing\n\n## Acceptance Criteria Checklist\n\n### FR-001: Validate YAML File Syntax\n- [ ] AC-1: Given a valid YAML file, the command reports it as valid\n- [ ] AC-2: Given an invalid YAML file, the command reports it as invalid with a descriptive error message\n- [ ] AC-3: Given multiple file paths, the command validates each file independently and reports results for all\n\n### FR-002: Provide Meaningful Error Messages\n- [ ] AC-1: Error output includes the file path that failed\n- [ ] AC-2: Error output includes a description of the syntax error (parser's native error message)\n- [ ] AC-3: If the parser provides a line number, it is included in the output (Note: HYP-002 rejected -- Bun.YAML.parse() does not provide line/column info; error messages will be generic)\n\n### FR-003: Return Appropriate Exit Codes\n- [ ] AC-1: Exit code is 0 when all files are valid YAML\n- [ ] AC-2: Exit code is non-zero when any file is invalid YAML\n- [ ] AC-3: Exit code is non-zero when any specified file does not exist or cannot be read\n\n### FR-004: Handle Missing or Unreadable Files\n- [ ] AC-1: A non-existent file path produces a clear \"file not found\" error message\n- [ ] AC-2: The command continues processing remaining files after encountering a missing file\n- [ ] AC-3: The overall exit code reflects the failure\n\n### FR-005: No New Dependencies\n- [ ] AC-1: The `package.json` `dependencies` field has no new entries\n- [ ] AC-2: The `package.json` `devDependencies` field has no new entries related to YAML parsing\n\n### FR-006: Display Usage Information\n- [ ] AC-1: Running with no file arguments displays a usage message describing expected input\n- [ ] AC-2: The usage message includes at least one example invocation\n\n### Business Rules\n- [ ] BR-001: Any file that cannot be parsed as valid YAML is reported as invalid\n- [ ] BR-002: Empty files are treated as valid YAML\n- [ ] BR-003: Multi-document YAML files are validated in their entirety\n- [ ] BR-004: The command is read-only; it never modifies any file on disk\n\n## Definition of Done\n\n- [ ] All tasks completed\n- [ ] All AC verified\n- [ ] Code reviewed\n- [ ] Docs updated\n"
