        "content": "# Design Decisions: YAML Validator Command\n\n**Feature ID**: yaml-validator-command\n**Created**: 2026-03-17\n\n## Decision Log\n\n| ID | Decision | Choice | Rationale | Alternatives Considered |\n|----|----------|--------|-----------|------------------------|\n| D1 | Module structure | Separate entry point (`validate-yaml.ts`) and logic module (`yaml-validator.ts`) | Follows existing project pattern where `index.ts` (entry) imports from `utils.ts` (logic). Enables testability of core logic without invoking CLI. | Single-file approach (rejected: harder to test, deviates from existing pattern) |\n| D2 | File reading API | `Bun.file(path).text()` | Bun-native API, async, efficient. No external deps needed. Consistent with Bun-first project philosophy. | `fs.readFileSync` (rejected: synchronous, Node-compat layer rather than Bun-native); `fs.promises.readFile` (rejected: Bun.file is more idiomatic) |\n| D3 | Multi-document YAML handling | Split content on `---` separator and validate each document individually | Satisfies BR-003 (all documents must be valid). Simple string splitting is sufficient for document boundary detection. | Single-parse approach (rejected: most parsers only return first document); Streaming parser (rejected: overkill for syntax validation) |\n| D4 | Output format | PASS/FAIL prefix with indented error details | Clear visual distinction between success and failure. Follows convention of test runners (familiar to developers). Summary line for multi-file runs. | JSON output (rejected: requirements specify human-readable; no structured output need stated); Verbose output (rejected: requirements say brief confirmation for valid files) |\n| D5 | YAML parsing abstraction | Isolate parsing behind `validateYamlContent` function | If Bun's built-in YAML parser has different API than expected, only this function needs to change. CLI layer and tests remain stable. | Direct parser calls throughout (rejected: tight coupling to specific parser API) |\n| D6 | Error message format | Include file path, error description, line/column when available | Satisfies FR-002 (meaningful errors). Line/column are conditionally included since parser may not always provide them. | Stack traces (rejected: too noisy for end users); Error codes (rejected: not needed for simple CLI tool) |\n| D7 | CLI argument parsing | Manual `process.argv.slice(2)` parsing | The argument structure is trivial (file paths + optional --help flag). No framework needed. Matches existing `src/index.ts` pattern exactly. | Commander.js or yargs (rejected: would add dependencies, violates FR-005); Bun's built-in arg parser if available (would be acceptable but manual parsing is simpler for this use case) |\n| D8 | Exit code strategy | 0 for all-pass, 1 for any-fail | Standard Unix convention. Simplest model that supports CI integration per FR-003. | Distinct codes per error type (rejected: unnecessary complexity; no requirement for it) |\n| D9 | Test file location | Co-located as `src/yaml-validator.test.ts` | Follows existing project pattern (`src/utils.test.ts`). Picked up by `bun test` automatically. | Separate `tests/` directory (rejected: deviates from existing co-location pattern) |\n| D10 | Script registration | `\"validate-yaml\": \"bun run src/validate-yaml.ts\"` in package.json | Follows existing script pattern (`\"dev\": \"bun run src/index.ts\"`). Provides npm-script-style invocation. | Binary registration in package.json `bin` field (rejected: overkill for project utility; not an installable CLI tool) |\n\n## AFK Mode: Auto-Selected Technology Decisions\n\n| Decision | Choice | Source | Rationale |\n|----------|--------|--------|-----------|\n| Runtime | Bun | KB index.md, architecture.md | Project is a Bun project; no other runtime considered |\n| Language | TypeScript strict mode | KB patterns.md | Project convention: \"TypeScript strict mode\" |\n| Module system | ESM | KB patterns.md | Project convention: \"ESM modules\" |\n| File naming | kebab-case | KB patterns.md | Project convention: \"Files: kebab-case TypeScript modules\" |\n| Function naming | camelCase | KB patterns.md | Project convention: \"Functions: camelCase\" |\n| Type naming | PascalCase | KB patterns.md | Project convention: \"Types: PascalCase\" |\n| Test runner | bun:test | KB patterns.md | Project convention: \"Bun's built-in test runner\" |\n| Test pattern | describe/test/expect | KB patterns.md | Project convention |\n| Test location | Co-located *.test.ts | KB patterns.md | Project convention: \"Tests co-located with source\" |\n| Error handling | try/catch with descriptive messages | KB patterns.md | Project convention: \"Simple try/catch with descriptive error messages\" |\n| File I/O | Bun.file() API | KB architecture.md | Bun-native API preferred over Node.js compat layer |\n| YAML parser | Bun built-in (to be validated) | Requirements assumption 4.3 | Constrained by FR-005 (no new deps) |\n"
